# oc-sim scenario v1
# TONE's input submenu (journal/D-036): as tone.scn up to the launch, then
# pick LEVEL, open its submenu and give it CV2 (ADD), left open, CV2 at one
# volt. The snapshot shows the frame over the main screen: LEVEL and the
# 1.6 V played in its top edge; CV2 in a lit box, the scale and the shift;
# MIN, MAX, EFFECT ADD, CENTER; the CV bar, 1 V as a band from 0 V; the VAL
# bar, the panel's 1 V a tick and 1.6 V a block.
ticks 300
20  button up down
60  button down down
70  button up up
70  button down up
90  button down down
100 button down up
110 button down down
120 button down up
130 button down down
140 button down up
150 button down down
160 button down up
180 button right down
186 button right up
200 encoder 1 +1
210 button right down
216 button right up
230 encoder 2 +2
250 cv 2 1000
